{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557860-what-s-everyone-s-favorite-storyteller-s-vault-supplements","id":1557860,"title":"What's everyone's favorite Storyteller's Vault supplements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-23T10:26:40-08:00","id":1557860,"title":"What's everyone's favorite Storyteller's Vault supplements?","content":"Hey all, I've been getting back into WoD again after a long time away so I've been a bit out of the loop and may be running a M20 game in the near future if the stars align.<br /> <br /> I was curious what ST Vault items you guys particularly liked. Any recommendations you'd give?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T07:16:21-08:00","id":1557875,"title":"","content":"I recommend Vampire: The Classical Era. A sourcebook about Kindred in the age of the Emperor Nero. I modified the setting to the period of the late Roman Republic, and it could probably be modified to run Mage as well (or any of the WoD games) if you wanted to put in the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T16:53:34-08:00","id":1557932,"title":"","content":"There are several good Mage books on Storytellers Vault. Without shilling my own books, I'd recommend:<br /> <br /> Sorcerer: Paths of Power and Riddle of the Sphinx are basically variations of M20 Sorcerer and Lore of the Traditions that came out before they did, and you might prefer over the official versions.<br /> Book of Common Magicks, Enlightened Grimoire, and Mystic Armory are good resources compiling effects, rotes, and wonders from previous editions.<br /> <br /> Book of Fragments and Foreign Magicks explore the minor spheres the Revised Storytellers Handbook<br /> <br /> It's not Mage, but I REALLY liked In the Realm of Gods and Dreams (for Changeling: the Dreaming)<br /> <br /> Also not Mage, but Umbral Pilots and the Shipyard might be useful if you're doing a lot of Deep Umbra/Void Engineer type stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T01:23:24-08:00","id":1557941,"title":"","content":"The <b>Paradigm Explored</b> series is very good. Also, don't neglect <b>Prism of Focus</b>; it's a huge help where a mage's Focus is concerned, with the only thing it <i>doesn't</i> touch upon being Instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T13:31:58-08:00","id":1557952,"title":"","content":"For me, it will be Tool of the trade and The paradigms progress. As both correct a massive blunder of M20. <br /> <br /> See, M20 wanted to correct the way paradigm was only surface level in previous editions. But in the end, while having a massive ammount of exemples of paradigms in the corebook, they are still just Roleplaying elements without impact on the games. <br /> <br /> Tool of the trade repairs that by develloping each M20 paradigms, associating them with systems and other way to impact the games in general. <br /> <br /> On the other side, worse than even revised, M20 is shy on ascension, you know, the big thing in the game's title. Even in brucato's Mage ade easy, he speaks on the importance on the quest for ascension, even though the edition on which he had basically free reign is lacking on that topic. <br /> <br /> Enter The paradigms progress, which also takes every M20 paradigm, give exemples on path to growth, both in term of ar\u00eate and of character, and toward ascension as a whole. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T21:12:53-08:00","id":1557978,"title":"","content":"I like the idea behind <b>Tools of the Trade</b> more than l like its implementation. In particular, I have two problems with it:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As written, every Component always either adds to or removes from your Arete roll; it never &quot;doesn't apply&quot;.</li> <li>It adjusts the size of the dice pool. This is something never done in published works, and Components don't strike me as the sort of thing in general that would justify adjusting the number of dice.</li> </ol>I personally prefer <b>Prism of Focus</b>' system of giving every Practice a strength and a weakness over <b>Tools of the Trade</b>'s Components system. But if I were to use the latter, I'd ditch the Banes entirely, or at the very least rework them so that they have their own conditions that need to be met, instead of merely being the complement of the Boon; and I'd have Boons (and, if kept, Banes) adjust the target number of an Arete roll, just like Magickal Modifiers. <br /> <br /> Another STV product which I find fascinating is <b>Stranger Magicks</b>, a book which introduces a system of Esoteric Experiences and Mysterial Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}